WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.240
Sometimes DNA test results can be confusing.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.620
For example, you might find that you and one

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.360
of your relatives don’t share any DNA.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.600
There are a couple of reasons for that.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.180
Maybe your family tree is actually

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.660
a little different from what you’ve been told.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.180
But sometimes it’s just biology —

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.060
specifically a process called recombination.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.180
That’s when chromosomes swap DNA.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.580
DNA contains the instructions for building your body.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.340
At the molecular level,

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.240
it’s shaped like a twisted ladder.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.520
Inside your cells,

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.340
these DNA ladders are arranged

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.220
in long strands called chromosomes.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:51.340
People usually have 23 pairs of chromosomes.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.460
Half of each pair comes from your mother

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.340
and the other half from your father.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.600
But long before egg meets sperm,

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.240
something interesting happens to your parents’ DNA

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:04.860
Inside the cells that become eggs or sperm,

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.200
chromosomes pair up.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.280
Pieces of DNA from one chromosome switch places

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.780
with pieces of DNA from the other chromosome.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.780
This swapping, or recombination, of DNA is important.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.140
It injects diversity into the mix and

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.600
ensures that you get just one copy

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.640
of each chromosome from each parent.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:27.660
Each generation does its own genetic shuffle.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.500
So grandma and grandpa each mix up the DNA

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.640
they inherited from your great-grandparents.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.400
Half of that recombined DNA

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.800
goes to your mom or dad.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:38.720
Then your parent’s DNA undergoes similar shuffling

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.720
before it’s passed on to you.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.160
To recap,

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:45.060
you inherit about 50 percent of each parent’s DNA

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.740
and about 25 percent of each grandparent’s DNA.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.780
But because you don’t get a carbon copy

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:55.840
of the DNA your parents inherited from their parents,

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.140
there’s some wiggle room in these numbers.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.920
Depending on where the recombination happens

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:01.960
on the chromosomes,

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.900
you could inherit a lot of DNA from your grandfather

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:07.360
and very little from your grandmother.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:10.920
So, you and your siblings end up with

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.500
different DNA mixes from your parents

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.520
(unless you’re identical twins).

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.780
And you and your cousins get different

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.520
genetic heirlooms from your grandparents.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:25.380
First and second cousins usually share DNA,

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.320
but because of recombination,

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:31.640
about 10 percent of third cousins won’t share any DNA.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.680
The same goes for about half of fourth cousins.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.080
That doesn’t mean you’re not related.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.680
You still have common family members,

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.040
and that counts as much or more

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.220
than having DNA in common.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:54.280
[music]

